### B4: a slow route as async def vs def (two requests at the same time)
$ s=$(date +%s.%N); curl -s localhost:19000/slow_async >/dev/null & curl -s localhost:19000/slow_async >/dev/null & wait; python3 -c "print('two requests to /slow_async took %.1f s' % ($(date +%s.%N) - $s))"
two requests to /slow_async took 4.0 s
[exit 0]

$ s=$(date +%s.%N); curl -s localhost:19000/slow_def >/dev/null & curl -s localhost:19000/slow_def >/dev/null & wait; python3 -c "print('two requests to /slow_def took %.1f s' % ($(date +%s.%N) - $s))"
two requests to /slow_def took 2.0 s
[exit 0]

### C6: CORS on v1 (CORSMiddleware allow_origins=['*']), and an unhandled error
$ curl -sS -i -H 'Origin: http://localhost:8080' http://localhost:19000/ | tr -d '\r' | grep -iE '^(HTTP|access-control)'
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
access-control-allow-origin: *
[exit 0]

$ curl -sS -i -X OPTIONS -H 'Origin: http://localhost:8080' -H 'Access-Control-Request-Method: POST' -H 'Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type,x-session-id' http://localhost:19000/square_root/ | tr -d '\r' | grep -iE '^(HTTP|access-control)'
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
access-control-allow-origin: *
access-control-allow-methods: DELETE, GET, HEAD, OPTIONS, PATCH, POST, PUT
access-control-max-age: 600
access-control-allow-headers: content-type,x-session-id
[exit 0]

